# Television k8s channels (k8s-pods-ns / k8s-deployments-ns / k8s-services-ns)
# read this file to decide which clusters + namespaces to show.
#
# One target per line:
#
#     <kube-context>  <namespace>
#
# - Lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# - Missing or unreachable contexts are skipped silently (like tmux-sessionizer paths).
# - This never uses --all-namespaces, so it's safe on locked-down clusters.
#
# Copy this to ~/.config/television/k8s-targets and edit for each machine.

rancher-desktop  default

# --- work clusters: uncomment & edit (contexts live in your work kubeconfig) ---
# sf-test  number-provisioning-beta
# au-test  number-provisioning-beta
